extends Node2D
## The level: shop -> storeroom -> stairs down -> the gas station's basement ->
## the boarded-up way into the tunnels -> zones 2, 3 and 4.
##
## The layout is ASCII so it can be tweaked in a text editor without a tile
## editor. Each character is one 16x16 tile:
##
##   #  solid (concrete zone)     .  concrete back wall (storeroom, open space)
##   %  solid (brick zone)        ,  brick back wall (tunnels, open space)
##                                :  ceramic-tiled back wall (the shop, open space)
##
## Markers sit on open space; their background copies the tile to their left.
##   P  player start               B  boarded panel (bottom cell of a 1x2 opening)
##   H  stairs (top-left, on the landing; the shaft below it is the stairwell)
##   W  Wedged Thing spawn         S  shelf of crisps (identical everywhere)
##   D  shop front door + EXIT     F  FUSE BOX sign       f  a wrong FUSE BOX sign
##   K  crisps shelf + "stack the shelf" job      R  drinks fridge + "check it" job
##   M  mop, bucket and the spill job             C  counter, till, CCTV (+ the torch)
##   X  breaker box (does nothing)
## The CCTV figure stands left of the front door D (only ever seen on camera).
##   1-9  triggers, configured in TRIGGERS below
##
## ROUND 2, PHASE 3: the underground is a NETWORK of short sections (15-30
## tiles), each in its own pocket of solid rock, connected by back-wall doors
## (press W: "backdoor" decor, use_door()), ladders between stacked sections
## ("ladder"), and the boarded panel. SECTIONS lists them; the map is generated
## by tools/gen_network.py (run it from the project folder). Length comes from the network and
## backtracking, not long corridors.
##
##   shop (Act 0) -> storeroom -> stairs down -> B1, the landing.
##   EVERY return trip comes back down to B1, a little different each time
##   (landmarks turned, missing, doubled), and the sealed "deeper" door in B1
##   now stands ajar onto the next zone.
##   zone 1: B1 landing (spiders) -> B2 crisps store (story, safe) -> B3 boiler
##           corridor (crouch-through, a dip) -> the boarded panel ->
##   zone 2: Z2-1 tunnel mouth (teaching arm; ladder up to Z2-2, the staff room)
##           -> Z2-3 long low tunnel (the eye) -> Z2-4 junction (the silhouette
##           crosses the work light) -> Z2-6 passage: the door's shut. Back to
##           Z2-4 -> Z2-5 pump room (the lever, the Cables, the cut-open cage)
##           -> Z2-6 again -> up-stair (trip 1).
##   zone 3a: A1 (Lure 1) -> A2 wet passage (floor arm, spiders) -> A3 the
##           Thing's room (ladder up to A4, the sleeping alcove) -> A5 the choice
##           (Lure 2 / the honest light over the up-stair, trip 2).
##   zone 3b: C1 (the leg) -> C2 monitor room (real arm) -> C3 the gallery (the
##           Thing) -> C4 lever room (timed door, Cable) -> up-stair (trip 3).
##   zone 4:  D1 -> D2 (Lure 3) -> D3 the climax -> D4 the squeeze, the end.
## Pacing (pacing.gd) adds tension, false alarms, silences ("hush" decor,
## before each encounter) and one safe room per zone ("safe" decor).

